  "slug": "number-of-sub-arrays-with-odd-sum",
  "title": "Number of Sub-arrays With Odd Sum",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "a subarray's sum is odd exactly when the prefix sum right before it and the prefix sum right after it have DIFFERENT parity - why?",
    "because subtracting two prefix sums of the same parity always gives an even result, and different parities always give an odd result",
    "keep two running counts as you scan: how many prefix sums seen so far (including the empty prefix, sum 0) are even, and how many are odd",
    "at each new prefix sum, if it's odd, it pairs with every EVEN prefix sum seen before to form odd subarrays (and vice versa) - add the appropriate counter to your answer, then update the counters, taking the modulo as you go"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to seed the even-count with 1 for the empty prefix (sum 0) before scanning starts",
    "not applying the modulo operation during accumulation, allowing overflow in languages with fixed-size integers",
    "mixing up which counter (even or odd) pairs with the current prefix sum's parity to produce an odd subarray"
  ],
  "content": {
